This solution uses two heaps to maintain the two halves of the sorted list of numbers. The `lower` heap is a max-heap (using negative values), and the `upper` heap is a min-heap. This allows us to efficiently get the median in constant time after each addition. The `add_num` method ensures that the heaps remain balanced, and the `find_median` method returns the appropriate median based on the sizes of the heaps.
